# Refuse to install under a Node that does not satisfy `engines` in package.json.
#
# npm's default is to print the mismatch as a warning and carry on, which is how
# this project spent a while appearing to have a broken test suite: run under
# Node 18, `npm test` reported "45 passed" and exited 1, because every
# `@vitest-environment jsdom` file crashed before collection. Two separate Node
# 18 limitations produce it — no `require()` of an ES module (jsdom's
# html-encoding-sniffer chain), and no resizable ArrayBuffer (webidl-conversions).
# Neither error mentions Node, so the obvious reading is "jsdom is broken" and
# the obvious fix is to start downgrading dependencies that were never at fault.
engine-strict=true
